{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}ROML core overhead — ROML model-build benchmark{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<h1>ROML Python naive chain / bulk / CSR vs native Rust core</h1>
<p>Both ROML Python paths and the native core build mathematically identical
models: same variables, constraints, coefficients, bounds, objective, and
naming policy (except the flat-namespace CSR ingestion arm, whose
per-element bounds are exact). The <strong>naive-chain-vs-core</strong>
comparison exposes expression-chaining cost — it is not a binding-overhead
measurement. The <strong>bulk-vs-core</strong> comparison answers how close
the public Python fast path gets to native construction, and the
<strong>named-vs-anonymous</strong> core comparison isolates eager
name-registration cost.</p>
{% for title, div in charts %}
<div class="chart"><h2>{{ title }}</h2>{{ div | safe }}</div>
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
